# fixedbugs, defect 2319, 2026-11-07: a group record naming every member of
# a wide C struct cost the compiler near the square of its members, at
# 2,048, 4,096 and 8,192 members 12.69, 38.16 and 130.19 billion
# instructions of its own as filed (the trunk's with defect 2288's repair;
# the trunk's alone 13.69, 42.29 and 146.76): the padding table's spans
# gathered by copying them at each member (defect 2284's repair), and the
# names a group binds, each field one, asked of its header through lists
# copied at each name (`cli/bound_names.hero`, `cli/pragma_ask.hero`,
# `cli/bound_ask.hero`).
# Each list now grows in place. This program's own build at `-O0` read
# 13.94 billion on the trunk's compiler, 10.77 after defect 2284's repair
# and 6.39 after this one. Each field holds its own value.
extern "fixedbugs-2319-a-group-record-naming-two-thousand-members-builds-in-linear-work.h"
    record Wide tag fixedbugs_2319_wide
        f0: u8
